1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,144
In today's lecture, I'm going to talk about Monosodium Glutamate,

2
00:00:05,144 --> 00:00:08,400
or MSG, as it's more commonly known.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:16,454
Now, MSG as you probably know, is a flavour enhancer which is used particularly in Chinese

4
00:00:16,454 --> 00:00:17,800
and Japanese cooking.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:23,616
Today I am going to explore why it is so popular in these cuisines

6
00:00:23,616 --> 00:00:28,650
and, more importantly, how does it enhance the flavour of food?

7
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:36,090
The main reason why MSG is more commonly used in Japanese meals is tradition.

8
00:00:36,090 --> 00:00:42,491
For many thousands of years the Japanese have incorporated a type of seaweed known

9
00:00:42,491 --> 00:00:47,406
as kombu in their cooking, as they discovered it had the ability to make

10
00:00:47,406 --> 00:00:48,530
food taste better.

11
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:55,446
But it wasn't until 1908 that the ingredient in kombu which was responsible for

12
00:00:55,446 --> 00:01:01,400
the improvement in flavour was actually discovered to be glutamate by scientists working there.

13
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:10,533
From 1908 until 1956, glutamate was produced commercially in Japan by a very slow

14
00:01:10,533 --> 00:01:12,600
and expensive means of extraction.

15
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:18,240
It was in 1956 that the speed of the process was improved,

16
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:23,720
and industrial production increased dramatically and still continues to increase to this day.

17
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:30,087
In fact, hundreds of thousands of tonnes of MSG are produced all over the

18
00:01:30,087 --> 00:01:30,690
world today.

19
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:34,800
So what exactly is MSG?

20
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:44,171
Well, Monosodium Glutamate contains seventy-eight point two per cent glutamate, twelve point two per cent sodium

21
00:01:44,171 --> 00:01:47,000
and nine point six per cent water.

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,602
Glutamate is an amino acid that can be found naturally in all protein-containing foods,

23
00:01:53,602 --> 00:01:54,646
erm,

24
00:01:54,646 --> 00:01:58,920
so this includes food such as meat and cheese.

25
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:04,234
It is widely known that Chinese and Japanese food contains MSG

26
00:02:04,234 --> 00:02:08,506
but many people don't seem to be aware that it is also used in

27
00:02:08,506 --> 00:02:09,970
foods in other parts of the world.

28
00:02:09,970 --> 00:02:17,094
For example it is found in commercially made Italian pizzas, in American fast food

29
00:02:17,094 --> 00:02:21,630
and in Britain MSG is used in things like potato crisps.

30
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:25,230
So, how exactly does MSG work?

31
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:30,523
Well, in the Western world, we commonly talk of four 'tastes',

32
00:02:30,523 --> 00:02:36,198
and I'm sure you're all familiar with the concepts of sweet, sour, bitter

33
00:02:36,198 --> 00:02:37,000
and salt.

34
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:43,350
Well, in 1908, Kikunae Ikeda identified a fifth 'taste'.

35
00:02:43,350 --> 00:02:50,470
And it is thought that MSG intensifies this naturally occurring 'taste' in some food.

36
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:56,329
It does make perfect evolutionary sense that we should have the ability to detect

37
00:02:56,329 --> 00:03:01,767
or taste glutamate because it is the amino acid which is most common in

38
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:02,630
natural foods.

39
00:03:02,630 --> 00:03:10,638
John Prescott, an associate professor at the University of Chicago, suggests that this fifth

40
00:03:10,638 --> 00:03:13,890
taste serves a purpose just as the other tastes do.

41
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:19,545
He suggests that it signals to us the presence of protein in food, in

42
00:03:19,545 --> 00:03:25,400
the same way that sweetness indicates that a food contains energy-giving carbohydrates.

43
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:29,592
Bitterness, he says, alerts us of toxins in the food,

44
00:03:29,592 --> 00:03:35,970
while sourness warns us of spoilage and saltiness signals the presence of minerals.

45
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:40,550
So, what else do we know about this fifth taste...
